---
/** Registration, once per session, and the path of one call. */
const arrow = (x1: number, y1: number, x2: number, y2: number) => `M${x1} ${y1} L${x2} ${y2}`;
---

<figure class="jam-diagram">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 880 330" role="img" aria-labelledby="tp-t tp-d">
    <title id="tp-t">Where a tool comes from, and what happens when the model calls one</title>
    <desc id="tp-d">
      Built-in tools, conditional tools and MCP server tools register into one registry per session. The tool set keeps
      the visible tools the permission engine offers, and produces the definitions sent with each request and the
      summaries that feed tool guidance. A call goes through the dispatcher's decision, then the registry checks
      the arguments against the schema, then the tool's runner runs.
    </desc>
    <g style="font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)" font-size="11.5" fill="currentColor">
      <text x="0" y="12" opacity="0.6">registration, once per session</text>

      <g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2">
        <rect x="0" y="24" width="210" height="44" />
        <rect x="0" y="80" width="210" height="44" stroke-dasharray="5 4" />
        <rect x="0" y="136" width="210" height="44" stroke-dasharray="5 4" />
        <rect x="260" y="80" width="150" height="44" />
        <rect x="460" y="80" width="180" height="44" style="stroke: var(--sl-color-accent)" stroke-width="1.6" />
        <rect x="690" y="24" width="190" height="44" />
        <rect x="690" y="136" width="190" height="44" />
        <path d={arrow(210, 46, 256, 96)} />
        <path d={arrow(210, 102, 256, 102)} />
        <path d={arrow(210, 158, 256, 108)} />
        <path d={arrow(410, 102, 456, 102)} />
        <path d={arrow(640, 94, 686, 50)} />
        <path d={arrow(640, 110, 686, 154)} />
      </g>
      <text x="12" y="43">BUILTIN_TOOLS</text>
      <text x="12" y="58" opacity="0.6">always</text>
      <text x="12" y="99">skill · lsp · web_search</text>
      <text x="12" y="114" opacity="0.6">search_tools · when they apply</text>
      <text x="12" y="155">MCP server tools</text>
      <text x="12" y="170" opacity="0.6">one entry per server tool</text>
      <text x="272" y="99">ToolRegistry</text>
      <text x="272" y="114" opacity="0.6">one per session</text>
      <text x="472" y="99">createToolSet()</text>
      <text x="472" y="114" opacity="0.6">visible and offered</text>
      <text x="702" y="43">definitions</text>
      <text x="702" y="58" opacity="0.6">sent with each request</text>
      <text x="702" y="155">summaries</text>
      <text x="702" y="170" opacity="0.6">feed toolGuidance()</text>

      <text x="0" y="226" opacity="0.6">one call</text>
      <g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2">
        <rect x="0" y="238" width="190" height="44" />
        <rect x="230" y="238" width="190" height="44" />
        <rect x="460" y="238" width="190" height="44" />
        <rect x="690" y="238" width="190" height="44" />
        <path d={arrow(190, 260, 226, 260)} />
        <path d={arrow(420, 260, 456, 260)} />
        <path d={arrow(650, 260, 686, 260)} />
      </g>
      <text x="12" y="257">model calls a tool</text>
      <text x="12" y="272" opacity="0.6">name + arguments</text>
      <text x="242" y="257">dispatcher.decide</text>
      <text x="242" y="272" opacity="0.6">mode + rules</text>
      <text x="472" y="257">registry.execute</text>
      <text x="472" y="272" opacity="0.6">arguments vs inputSchema</text>
      <text x="702" y="257">runner(args, ctx)</text>
      <text x="702" y="272" opacity="0.6">returns output</text>
      <text x="242" y="306" opacity="0.6">allow, ask, or deny</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>Dashed sources register only when their condition holds. Everything after the registry is generic: it treats a new tool the same as the existing ones.</figcaption>
</figure>
